attleground: Adam Hamilton has dramatically out-raised Marshall, and outside groups have spent heavily against the incumbent, including ads about his medical-debt lawsuits.\n\nPolling in the final week consistently shows Hamilton ahead, with margins ranging from one point to nine points and an average near four points for the Democrat. Expert raters are split between Tossup and Lean D, with several flagging the seat as a potential flip. A favorable national environment for Democrats compounds Marshall's vulnerability, though the state's partisan baseline keeps this well short of safe for either side.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2893, "margin": -2.76}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3585, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4222, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4301, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3024, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2988, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4183, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4225, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3457, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4294, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3861, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3969, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4021, "margin": -1.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3351, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3274, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.4309, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3899, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3704, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.3611, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.3573, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.4584, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.4244, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.4264, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.4319, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": 